    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a conflict-of-interest checker for a US law firm.\n\nPROSPECTIVE CLIENT\n- Name: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.full_name }}\n- Opposing party: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.opposing_party }}\n\nFIRM CLIENT DATABASE (JSON)\n{{ JSON.stringify($json.clients) }}\n\nRULES\n1. CONFLICT: the opposing party is the same person or company as any \"client_name\" in the database (active or closed).\n2. CONFLICT: the prospective client's name is the same as any \"opposing_party\" in the database.\n3. RELATED MATTER: no conflict, but the opposing party is the same as an \"opposing_party\" in the database (the firm already represents someone against that party).\n4. CLEAR: none of the above.\n\nIf the opposing party is \"No opposing party\", only check rule 2.\nTreat names as the same if they only differ in capitalization, punctuation or suffixes like LLC, Inc, Co, Corp, Group.\nDo not guess: people who only share a last name are NOT a match.\n\nReturn the matched client_id values and a one-sentence reason written for an attorney.",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        816,
        0
      ],
      "id": "08aa0713-6d9f-4a3a-83d1-8d2d3e8911d8",
      "name": "Conflict Check (AI)",
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "waitBetweenTries": 5000
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=You are a legal intake assistant for a US law firm. Your job is to prepare a short case evaluation for an attorney. You never give legal advice and never promise outcomes.\n\nFIRM PRACTICE AREAS: Personal Injury, Family Law, Employment Law, Business Law, Real Estate, Estate Planning.\n\nINTAKE SUBMISSION\n- Name: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.full_name }}\n- Practice area selected: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.practice_area }}\n- Opposing party: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.opposing_party }}\n- What happened: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.description }}\n- Date of incident: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.incident_date }}\n- Upcoming court date or deadline: {{ $('Normalize Intake Data').first().json.upcoming_deadline }}\n\nCONFLICT CHECK RESULT\n- Status: {{ $json.output.conflict_status }}\n- Details: {{ $json.output.conflict_reason }}\n\nINSTRUCTIONS\n1. case_summary: 2-3 sentences, neutral and factual, written for an attorney.\n2. key_facts: the most relevant facts as a short list (parties, amounts, injuries, dates).\n3. urgency:\n   - \"High\" if there is an upcoming court date or deadline, or the facts suggest a time-sensitive matter (recent injury, eviction, custody emergency).\n   - \"Medium\" if the deadline answer is \"Not sure\".\n   - \"Low\" otherwise.\n4. case_quality:\n   - \"Qualified\": the issue fits a firm practice area, the opposing party is identifiable and there is clear harm or damages.\n   - \"Needs Review\": facts are unclear, incomplete, or the selected practice area does not match the description.\n   - \"Not a Fit\": the issue is outside the firm's practice areas or there is no apparent legal issue.\n5. recommended_next_step: one sentence for the attorney. If the conflict status is \"CONFLICT\", it must be: \"Do not proceed until the conflict is reviewed by the responsible attorney.\"",
        "hasOutputParser": true,
        "batching": {}
      },
      "type": "@n8n/n8n-nodes-langchain.chainLlm",
      "typeVersion": 1.9,
      "position": [
        1168,
        0
      ],
      "id": "3374d952-da5c-4f89-a39a-1c93eb57b160",
